      "responseId": "response_0645b4ab-144c-49d1-9179-37c725b09ffa",
      "result": {
        "timings": {
          "firstProgress": 1213,
          "totalElapsed": 6742
        },
        "metadata": {
          "codeBlocks": [
            {
              "code": "### Example Workspace Configuration\n\nBelow is an example of a `.code-workspace` file configuration for Visual Studio Code:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"folders\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \".\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"settings\": {\n    \"dotnet-test-explorer.testProjectPath\": \"{workspacefolder}/tests\",\n    \"pester.pesterModulePath\": \"{workspacefolder}\",\n    \"powershell.pester.codeLens\": false,\n    \"powershell.pester.useLegacyCodeLens\": false,\n    \"powershell.pester.outputVerbosity\": \"Diagnostic\",\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.autoCorrectAliases\": true,\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.avoidSemicolonsAsLineTerminators\": true,\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.newLineAfterCloseBrace\": false,\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.newLineAfterOpenBrace\": false,\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.pipelineIndentationStyle\": \"IncreaseIndentationForFirstPipeline\",\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.trimWhitespaceAroundPipe\": true,\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.useConstantStrings\": true,\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.useCorrectCasing\": true,\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.whitespaceBetweenParameters\": true,\n    \"powershell.enableProfileLoading\": true\n  }\n}\n```\n",
              "language": "markdown",
              "markdownBeforeBlock": "To implement the here-doc containing the JSON configuration into your  file, you can follow these steps:\n\n### 1. **Decide Placement**\nDetermine where in the  file you want to include the JSON configuration. Based on the provided content, it seems logical to place it under a relevant section, such as **\"Symbolic Links for VSC settings, tasks, launch configurations, and testing\"**.\n\n### 2. **Insert the Here-Doc**\nAdd the JSON configuration as a code block in Markdown format. Here's how it would look:\n\n"
            },
            {
              "code": "git add ReadMe.md\ngit commit -m \"Added example workspace configuration to ReadMe.md\"\ngit push\n",
              "language": "bash",
              "markdownBeforeBlock": "\n### 3. **Save and Commit**\nAfter adding the JSON configuration, save the file and commit the changes to your repository:\n\n"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [
            {
              "role": "user",
              "content": "How do I implement this?"
            },
            {
              "role": "assistant",
              "content": "To implement the here-doc containing the JSON configuration into your `ReadMe.md` file, you can follow these steps:\n\n### 1. **Decide Placement**\nDetermine where in the `ReadMe.md` file you want to include the JSON configuration. Based on the provided content, it seems logical to place it under a relevant section, such as **\"Symbolic Links for VSC settings, tasks, launch configurations, and testing\"**.\n\n### 2. **Insert the Here-Doc**\nAdd the JSON configuration as a code block in Markdown format. Here's how it would look:\n\n````markdown\n### Example Workspace Configuration\n\nBelow is an example of a `.code-workspace` file configuration for Visual Studio Code:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"folders\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \".\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"settings\": {\n    \"dotnet-test-explorer.testProjectPath\": \"{workspacefolder}/tests\",\n    \"pester.pesterModulePath\": \"{workspacefolder}\",\n    \"powershell.pester.codeLens\": false,\n    \"powershell.pester.useLegacyCodeLens\": false,\n    \"powershell.pester.outputVerbosity\": \"Diagnostic\",\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.autoCorrectAliases\": true,\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.avoidSemicolonsAsLineTerminators\": true,\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.newLineAfterCloseBrace\": false,\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.newLineAfterOpenBrace\": false,\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.pipelineIndentationStyle\": \"IncreaseIndentationForFirstPipeline\",\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.trimWhitespaceAroundPipe\": true,\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.useConstantStrings\": true,\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.useCorrectCasing\": true,\n    \"powershell.codeFormatting.whitespaceBetweenParameters\": true,\n    \"powershell.enableProfileLoading\": true\n  }\n}\n```\n````\n\n### 3. **Save and Commit**\nAfter adding the JSON configuration, save the file and commit the changes to your repository:\n\n```bash\ngit add ReadMe.md\ngit commit -m \"Added example workspace configuration to ReadMe.md\"\ngit push\n```\n\nThis will ensure the configuration is documented and available for reference in your repository."
            }
          ],
          "modelMessageId": "268335a0-4083-4eb1-b1cc-6b6fce04e0fd",
