            "scheme": "file"
          }
        },
        {
          "value": " file. Ensure there are no duplicate entries or conflicting names.\n\nFor example:\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"version\": \"0.2.0\",\n  \"configurations\": [\n    // Configurations from File 1\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Launch App 1\",\n      \"type\": \"node\",\n      \"request\": \"launch\",\n      \"program\": \"${workspaceFolder}/app1.js\",\n      \"console\": \"integratedTerminal\"\n    },\n    // Configurations from File 2\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Launch App 2\",\n      \"type\": \"node\",\n      \"request\": \"launch\",\n      \"program\": \"${workspaceFolder}/app2.js\",\n      \"console\": \"integratedTerminal\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### 3. **Use Comments for Organization**\nIf you are merging configurations from different projects or purposes, use comments to separate and document them.\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"version\": \"0.2.0\",\n  \"configurations\": [\n    // Configurations for Project A\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Launch Project A\",\n      \"type\": \"node\",\n      \"request\": \"launch\",\n      \"program\": \"${workspaceFolder}/projectA/index.js\",\n      \"console\": \"integratedTerminal\"\n    },\n    // Configurations for Project B\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Launch Project B\",\n      \"type\": \"node\",\n      \"request\": \"launch\",\n      \"program\": \"${workspaceFolder}/projectB/index.js\",\n      \"console\": \"integratedTerminal\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### 4. **Automate with a Script (Optional)**\nIf you have many ",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
