        "metadata": {
          "codeBlocks": [
            {
              "code": "param (\n  [string] $repoPath = 'C:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities',\n  [string] $outputFile = 'C:\\temp\\embeddings.json',\n  [string[]] $targetExtensions = @(\".cs\", \".ps1\", \".ts\", \".js\", \".md\", \".json\", \".jsonc\", \".xml\", \".yaml\", \".yml\", \".txt\"),\n  [string[]] $excludedDirs = @(\"__generated\", \"bin\", \"obj\")\n)\n",
              "language": "powershell",
              "markdownBeforeBlock": "When running a PowerShell script in Visual Studio Code under the debugger, the default values for parameters in the `param` block are not automatically used. Instead, the debugger prompts for user input for all mandatory parameters. This behavior occurs because the debugger treats the script as if it is being invoked without any arguments, and mandatory parameters must be provided.\n\n### Solution: Provide Default Values or Arguments in the Debugger\n\n#### 1. **Modify the `param` Block to Make Parameters Optional**\nIf you want the script to use the default values without prompting, remove the `Mandatory = $true` attribute for the parameters:\n\n"
            },
            {
              "code": "{\n  \"type\": \"PowerShell\",\n  \"request\": \"launch\",\n  \"name\": \"Run Get-FilesFromRepository.ps1\",\n  \"script\": \"${file}\",\n  \"args\": [\n    \"-repoPath\", \"C:\\\\Dropbox\\\\whertzing\\\\GitHub\\\\ATAP.Utilities\",\n    \"-outputFile\", \"C:\\\\temp\\\\embeddings.json\",\n    \"-targetExtensions\", \".cs\", \".ps1\", \".ts\", \".js\", \".md\", \".json\", \".jsonc\", \".xml\", \".yaml\", \".yml\", \".txt\",\n    \"-excludedDirs\", \"__generated\", \"bin\", \"obj\"\n  ]\n}\n",
              "language": "json",
              "markdownBeforeBlock": "\nThis way, the script will use the default values if no arguments are provided.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. **Pass Arguments in the Debugger Configuration**\nYou can pass arguments to the script in the `launch.json` file for the debugger. Here's how:\n\n1. Open the  file.\n2. Add or modify the configuration for your script to include the `args` property.\n\nExample `launch.json` configuration:\n"
            },
            {
              "code": ".\\Get-FilesFromRepository.ps1\n",
              "language": "powershell",
              "markdownBeforeBlock": "\nWhen you run the debugger, these arguments will be passed to the script, and the debugger will not prompt for input.\n\n---\n\n#### 3. **Use Default Values in Debugging**\nIf you want to keep the `Mandatory = $true` attribute but avoid being prompted during debugging, you can provide default values in the `args` property of the `launch.json` file, as shown above.\n\n---\n\n#### 4. **Run the Script Outside the Debugger**\nIf you don't need to debug the script, you can run it directly in the integrated terminal. The default values will be used without prompting for input:\n\n"
            }
