        {
          "value": "The error occurs because the `ForEach-Object -Parallel` block is being used incorrectly. The issue is related to the parameters provided to the `-Parallel` parameter set of the `ForEach-Object` cmdlet. Here's a breakdown of the problem and how to fix it:\n\n---\n\n### **Cause of the Error**\n\n1. **Incorrect Parameter Usage**:\n   - The `-Parallel` parameter set of `ForEach-Object` requires specific parameters to be used together. In this case, the `-ArgumentList` parameter is being used, but it is not properly defined or passed to the parallel script block.\n\n2. **Missing or Incorrect Parameter Passing**:\n   - The `-ArgumentList` parameter is used to pass additional arguments to the parallel script block. However, in the provided code, the variables `$apiKey` and `$embeddingModel` are not defined or passed correctly to the script block.\n\n3. **PowerShell Version**:\n   - The `-Parallel` parameter is only available in PowerShell 7.0 or later. If you are running this script in an older version of PowerShell, the `-Parallel` parameter will not work.\n\n---\n\n### **Fixes**\n\n#### 1. **Ensure PowerShell 7+ is Installed**\n   - Verify that you are running PowerShell 7 or later by checking the version:\n     ```powershell\n     $PSVersionTable.PSVersion\n     ```\n   - If you are not using PowerShell 7+, install it from [PowerShell GitHub Releases](https://github.com/PowerShell/PowerShell).\n\n---\n\n#### 2. **Properly Define and Pass Arguments**\n   - Ensure that `$apiKey` and `$embeddingModel` are defined before the `ForEach-Object -Parallel` block.\n   - Pass these variables correctly using the `-ArgumentList` parameter.\n\n   Example:\n   ```powershell\n   $apiKey = \"YourApiKey\"\n   $embeddingModel = \"YourEmbeddingModel\"\n\n   $allFiles | ForEach-Object -Parallel {\n       param($file, $apiKey, $embeddingModel)\n       $content = Get-Content $file.FullName -Raw\n       if ($content.Length -lt 8192) {\n           $filesToBeProcessed.Add($file.FullName)\n       }\n       else {\n           $longFiles.Add($file.FullName)\n       }\n   } -ArgumentList $apiKey, $embeddingModel -ThrottleLimit 8\n   ```\n\n   **Explanation**:\n   - The `param` block inside the `-Parallel` script block must explicitly declare the parameters being passed via `-ArgumentList`.\n   - The `-ArgumentList` parameter must match the order of the parameters in the `param` block.\n\n---\n\n#### 3. **Remove Unnecessary Parameters if Not Needed**\n   - If `$apiKey` and `$embeddingModel` are not required, you can remove the `-ArgumentList` parameter entirely.\n\n   Example:\n   ```powershell\n   $allFiles | ForEach-Object -Parallel {\n       param($file)\n       $content = Get-Content $file.FullName -Raw\n       if ($content.Length -lt 8192) {\n           $filesToBeProcessed.Add($file.FullName)\n       }\n       else {\n           $longFiles.Add($file.FullName)\n       }\n   } -ThrottleLimit 8\n   ```\n\n---\n\n#### 4. **Debugging the Issue**\n   - Add debug messages to ensure that `$allFiles` contains valid data and that the script block is receiving the correct inputs.\n\n   Example:\n   ```powershell\n   Write-Host \"Processing file: $file.FullName\"\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### **Final Corrected Code**\nHere is the corrected version of your script:\n\n```powershell\n# Ensure $apiKey and $embeddingModel are defined\n$api",
