              "role": "user",
              "content": "what version of powershell"
            },
            {
              "role": "assistant",
              "content": "The `-Parallel` parameter of the `ForEach-Object` cmdlet is only available in **PowerShell 7.0** or later. To check your current PowerShell version, run the following command:\n\n```powershell\n$PSVersionTable.PSVersion\n```\n\n### Expected Output:\nThe output will look something like this:\n\n```plaintext\nMajor  Minor  Build  Revision\n-----  -----  -----  --------\n7      3      0      0\n```\n\nIf the `Major` version is **less than 7**, you are using an older version of PowerShell that does not support the `-Parallel` parameter.\n\n---\n\n### **What to Do If You Are Using an Older Version**\n1. **Install PowerShell 7+**:\n   - Download and install the latest version of PowerShell from the [PowerShell GitHub Releases page](https://github.com/PowerShell/PowerShell/releases).\n\n2. **Run the Script in PowerShell 7**:\n   - After installation, launch PowerShell 7 by searching for `pwsh` in your system or running it from the terminal.\n\n3. **Verify the Version**:\n   - Run `$PSVersionTable.PSVersion` again in the new PowerShell session to confirm you are using version 7 or later.\n\n---\n\n### **If You Are Already Using PowerShell 7+**\nIf you are using PowerShell 7+ and still encountering issues, ensure that:\n- The `ForEach-Object -Parallel` syntax is correct.\n- All required parameters are properly passed to the `-Parallel` block."
            }
          ],
