      "response": [
        {
          "value": "To configure the GELF logging provider to use **UDP** instead of **TCP**, you can update the configuration as follows:\n\n### Updated Configuration for UDP\n```powershell\n$gelfLoggingProviderConfiguration = @{\n    Name = 'gelf'\n    GelfServer = '127.0.0.1'\n    Port = 12201\n    Protocol = 'udp'  # Set protocol to UDP\n    Encrypt = $false\n    MinLevel = 6\n    Enabled = $true\n    Verbose = $true\n}\nSet-PSFLoggingProvider @gelfLoggingProviderConfiguration\nSet-PSFLoggingProvider -Name gelf -Enabled $true\n\n# Explicitly initialize the logging provider\n$null = Wait-PSFMessage -Timeout 1\n\n# Verify the configuration\nGet-PSFLoggingProvider -Name gelf | Format-List\n```\n\n### Explanation of Changes\n1. **Protocol**:\n   - The `Protocol` key is explicitly set to `'udp'` to ensure the GELF provider uses UDP for communication.\n\n2. **Initialization**:\n   - The `Wait-PSFMessage` cmdlet ensures the provider is initialized and ready to log messages.\n\n3. **Verification**:\n   - Use `Get-PSFLoggingProvider` to confirm that the provider is configured correctly and initialized.\n\n---\n\n### Additional Notes\n- UDP is the default protocol for the GELF provider, so explicitly setting it is optional unless it was previously overridden to use TCP.\n- Ensure that the target server (e.g., Graylog or SEQ) is configured to listen for GELF messages on `udp://127.0.0.1:12201`.\n\nThis configuration ensures that the GELF logging provider uses UDP for sending log messages.",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        }
      ],
      "responseId": "response_16f936f2-d3ac-473d-b2b0-26a879f269eb",
      "result": {
        "timings": {
          "firstProgress": 3102,
          "totalElapsed": 8446
        },
        "metadata": {
          "codeBlocks": [
            {
              "code": "$gelfLoggingProviderConfiguration = @{\n    Name = 'gelf'\n    GelfServer = '127.0.0.1'\n    Port = 12201\n    Protocol = 'udp'  # Set protocol to UDP\n    Encrypt = $false\n    MinLevel = 6\n    Enabled = $true\n    Verbose = $true\n}\nSet-PSFLoggingProvider @gelfLoggingProviderConfiguration\nSet-PSFLoggingProvider -Name gelf -Enabled $true\n\n# Explicitly initialize the logging provider\n$null = Wait-PSFMessage -Timeout 1\n\n# Verify the configuration\nGet-PSFLoggingProvider -Name gelf | Format-List\n",
              "language": "powershell",
              "markdownBeforeBlock": "To configure the GELF logging provider to use **UDP** instead of **TCP**, you can update the configuration as follows:\n\n### Updated Configuration for UDP\n"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [
            {
              "role": "user",
              "content": "use udp not tcp"
            },
            {
              "role": "assistant",
              "content": "To configure the GELF logging provider to use **UDP** instead of **TCP**, you can update the configuration as follows:\n\n### Updated Configuration for UDP\n```powershell\n$gelfLoggingProviderConfiguration = @{\n    Name = 'gelf'\n    GelfServer = '127.0.0.1'\n    Port = 12201\n    Protocol = 'udp'  # Set protocol to UDP\n    Encrypt = $false\n    MinLevel = 6\n    Enabled = $true\n    Verbose = $true\n}\nSet-PSFLoggingProvider @gelfLoggingProviderConfiguration\nSet-PSFLoggingProvider -Name gelf -Enabled $true\n\n# Explicitly initialize the logging provider\n$null = Wait-PSFMessage -Timeout 1\n\n# Verify the configuration\nGet-PSFLoggingProvider -Name gelf | Format-List\n```\n\n### Explanation of Changes\n1. **Protocol**:\n   - The `Protocol` key is explicitly set to `'udp'` to ensure the GELF provider uses UDP for communication.\n\n2. **Initialization**:\n   - The `Wait-PSFMessage` cmdlet ensures the provider is initialized and ready to log messages.\n\n3. **Verification**:\n   - Use `Get-PSFLoggingProvider` to confirm that the provider is configured correctly and initialized.\n\n---\n\n### Additional Notes\n- UDP is the default protocol for the GELF provider, so explicitly setting it is optional unless it was previously overridden to use TCP.\n- Ensure that the target server (e.g., Graylog or SEQ) is configured to listen for GELF messages on `udp://127.0.0.1:12201`.\n\nThis configuration ensures that the GELF logging provider uses UDP for sending log messages."
            }
          ],
          "modelMessageId": "7216e0cb-be79-4353-88c8-84c877a9be30",
