      "response": [
        {
          "value": "To find out the `minlevel` and `maxlevel` for the **console** logging provider in PSFramework, you can use the following commands:\n\n```powershell\nGet-PSFConfig 'PSFramework.Logging.Console.MinLevel'\nGet-PSFConfig 'PSFramework.Logging.Console.MaxLevel'\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n- **`PSFramework.Logging.Console.MinLevel`**: This configuration determines the minimum log level that will be written to the console.\n- **`PSFramework.Logging.Console.MaxLevel`**: This configuration determines the maximum log level that will be written to the console.\n\n### Example Output:\n```plaintext\nName                           Value\n----                           -----\nPSFramework.Logging.Console.MinLevel 0\nPSFramework.Logging.Console.MaxLevel 9\n```\n\n### Additional Notes:\n- Log levels typically range from `0` (Verbose) to `9` (Critical).\n- You can adjust these levels using the `Set-PSFConfig` cmdlet if needed:\n  ```powershell\n  Set-PSFConfig 'PSFramework.Logging.Console.MinLevel' 2\n  Set-PSFConfig 'PSFramework.Logging.Console.MaxLevel' 7\n  ```\n\nThis will ensure that only log messages within the specified range are written to the console.",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        }
      ],
      "responseId": "response_3b05ffc0-d2b4-445c-b1d4-e9f2c1ee091c",
      "result": {
        "timings": {
          "firstProgress": 4304,
          "totalElapsed": 7975
        },
        "metadata": {
          "codeBlocks": [
            {
              "code": "Get-PSFConfig 'PSFramework.Logging.Console.MinLevel'\nGet-PSFConfig 'PSFramework.Logging.Console.MaxLevel'\n",
              "language": "powershell",
              "markdownBeforeBlock": "To find out the `minlevel` and `maxlevel` for the **console** logging provider in PSFramework, you can use the following commands:\n\n"
            },
            {
              "code": "Name                           Value\n----                           -----\nPSFramework.Logging.Console.MinLevel 0\nPSFramework.Logging.Console.MaxLevel 9\n",
              "language": "plaintext",
              "markdownBeforeBlock": "\n### Explanation:\n- **`PSFramework.Logging.Console.MinLevel`**: This configuration determines the minimum log level that will be written to the console.\n- **`PSFramework.Logging.Console.MaxLevel`**: This configuration determines the maximum log level that will be written to the console.\n\n### Example Output:\n"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [
            {
              "role": "user",
              "content": "how do i find out the minlevel and maxlevel for the console provider"
            },
            {
              "role": "assistant",
              "content": "To find out the `minlevel` and `maxlevel` for the **console** logging provider in PSFramework, you can use the following commands:\n\n```powershell\nGet-PSFConfig 'PSFramework.Logging.Console.MinLevel'\nGet-PSFConfig 'PSFramework.Logging.Console.MaxLevel'\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n- **`PSFramework.Logging.Console.MinLevel`**: This configuration determines the minimum log level that will be written to the console.\n- **`PSFramework.Logging.Console.MaxLevel`**: This configuration determines the maximum log level that will be written to the console.\n\n### Example Output:\n```plaintext\nName                           Value\n----                           -----\nPSFramework.Logging.Console.MinLevel 0\nPSFramework.Logging.Console.MaxLevel 9\n```\n\n### Additional Notes:\n- Log levels typically range from `0` (Verbose) to `9` (Critical).\n- You can adjust these levels using the `Set-PSFConfig` cmdlet if needed:\n  ```powershell\n  Set-PSFConfig 'PSFramework.Logging.Console.MinLevel' 2\n  Set-PSFConfig 'PSFramework.Logging.Console.MaxLevel' 7\n  ```\n\nThis will ensure that only log messages within the specified range are written to the console."
            }
          ],
