          "value": ") when running `Invoke-Pester`, you can use the `-ExcludePath` parameter with a comma-separated list of paths or patterns. Here's how you can modify your command:\n\n```powershell\nInvoke-Pester -Path C:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.Powershell `\n  -ExcludePath */Resources/*, */Releases/* `\n  -OutputFormat NUnitXml `\n  -OutputFile C:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.Powershell\\_generated\\TestResults\\results.xml\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n1. **`-ExcludePath`**:\n   - The `-ExcludePath` parameter accepts multiple paths or patterns separated by commas.\n   - Each pattern (e.g., `*/Resources/*` or `*/Releases/*`) excludes matching directories or files.\n\n2. **Wildcards**:\n   - `*` matches any number of characters.\n   - `*/Resources/*` excludes all files and subdirectories under any ",
