            {
              "code": "$results = Invoke-Pester -Path C:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.Powershell `\n  -ExcludePath */Resources/*, */Releases/* `\n  -PassThru\n\n$results.Tests | Where-Object { $_.Path -match 'Resources|Releases' }\n",
              "language": "powershell",
              "markdownBeforeBlock": "\n### Explanation:\n1. **`-ExcludePath`**:\n   - The `-ExcludePath` parameter accepts multiple paths or patterns separated by commas.\n   - Each pattern (e.g., `*/Resources/*` or `*/Releases/*`) excludes matching directories or files.\n\n2. **Wildcards**:\n   - `*` matches any number of characters.\n   - `*/Resources/*` excludes all files and subdirectories under any  directory.\n   - `*/Releases/*` excludes all files and subdirectories under any  directory.\n\n3. **Backticks (`) for Line Continuation**:\n   - The backtick (`) is used to split the command across multiple lines for readability.\n\n### Verifying Exclusions:\nTo confirm that the exclusions are working, you can run `Invoke-Pester` with the `-PassThru` parameter and inspect the results:\n\n"
