          "messages": [
            {
              "role": "user",
              "content": "this command\r\nPowerShell\\ > \r\nElevated  HOST:utat022  USER:whertzing .\\ATAP.Utilities.Powershell\\ > . {\r\nInvoke-Pester\r\n} -Path C:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.Powershell -ExcludePath */Resources/* -OutputFormat NUnitXml -OutputFile C:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.Powershell/_generated/TestResults/results.xml \r\nis finding and runnig tests in a subdirecotry below '/resources/ called 'releases'. how can I exclude two directories?"
            },
            {
              "role": "assistant",
              "content": "To exclude multiple directories (e.g., `Resources` and `Releases`) when running `Invoke-Pester`, you can use the `-ExcludePath` parameter with a comma-separated list of paths or patterns. Here's how you can modify your command:\n\n```powershell\nInvoke-Pester -Path C:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.Powershell `\n  -ExcludePath */Resources/*, */Releases/* `\n  -OutputFormat NUnitXml `\n  -OutputFile C:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.Powershell\\_generated\\TestResults\\results.xml\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n1. **`-ExcludePath`**:\n   - The `-ExcludePath` parameter accepts multiple paths or patterns separated by commas.\n   - Each pattern (e.g., `*/Resources/*` or `*/Releases/*`) excludes matching directories or files.\n\n2. **Wildcards**:\n   - `*` matches any number of characters.\n   - `*/Resources/*` excludes all files and subdirectories under any `Resources` directory.\n   - `*/Releases/*` excludes all files and subdirectories under any `Releases` directory.\n\n3. **Backticks (`) for Line Continuation**:\n   - The backtick (`) is used to split the command across multiple lines for readability.\n\n### Verifying Exclusions:\nTo confirm that the exclusions are working, you can run `Invoke-Pester` with the `-PassThru` parameter and inspect the results:\n\n```powershell\n$results = Invoke-Pester -Path C:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.Powershell `\n  -ExcludePath */Resources/*, */Releases/* `\n  -PassThru\n\n$results.Tests | Where-Object { $_.Path -match 'Resources|Releases' }\n```\n\nIf the exclusions are working correctly, the output should not include any tests from the `Resources` or `Releases` directories.\n\n### Notes:\n- Ensure that the paths you specify in `-ExcludePath` match the actual directory structure.\n- If the exclusions are not working as expected, double-check the directory names and patterns."
            }
          ],
