          "value": "The most appropriate PowerShell verb to instruct a 3rd party app to create something is **`New`**.\n\n### Reason:\n- The [`New`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/scripting/developer/cmdlet/approved-verbs-for-windows-powershell-commands?view=powershell-7.4#creation-verbs) verb is the standard, approved verb in PowerShell for creating new resources, objects, or entities.\n- It is clear, concise, and aligns with PowerShell best practices and user expectations.\n\n**Example:**  \n`New-Resource`, `New-Feed`, `New-Item`, `New-User`, etc.\n\n> Use `New` unless the creation is specifically a copy of something else (then use `Copy`), or if you are restoring from a backup (then use `Restore`). For general creation, `New` is the best choice.",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/",
