      "response": [
        {
          "value": "The most appropriate PowerShell verb to instruct a 3rd party app to **delete** something is **`Remove`**.\n\n---\n\n**Reason:**  \n`Remove` is the approved PowerShell verb for deleting or eliminating resources, objects, or entities.  \nIt is clear, standard, and aligns with PowerShell best practices.\n\n**Examples:**  \n- `Remove-Item` (deletes a file or folder)\n- `Remove-User`\n- `Remove-Feed`\n- `Remove-PackageRepositoryFeed`\n\n> Use `Remove` for deletion operations in your cmdlet/function names when instructing a 3rd party app to delete something.",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
