          "toolCallRounds": [
            {
              "response": "Yes, you can search for a file by its name in Visual Studio Code in a multiroot repository.\n\n### How to do it:\n1. **Press** `Ctrl+P` (or `Cmd+P` on Mac)  \n   This opens the Quick Open dialog.\n\n2. **Type the file name** (or part of it)  \n   VS Code will show matching files from all folders in your workspace, including all roots in a multiroot setup.\n\n3. **Select the file** from the list to open it.\n\n---\n\n**Tip:**  \nYou can also use the sidebar search (`Ctrl+Shift+F`) and set the search to look for files by name using the `files to include` field, or use the file explorer to browse all folders.",
