      "response": [
        {
          "value": "Here’s a typical workflow on the command line to merge your current bug-fix branch back into `main`:\n\n````bash\n# 1. Make sure your bug branch is up to date\ngit checkout bug-branch\ngit pull origin bug-branch\n\n# 2. Switch to main and update\ngit checkout main\ngit pull origin main\n\n# 3. Merge the bug branch into main\ngit merge bug-branch\n\n# 4. Resolve any conflicts, then:\ngit add <resolved-files>\ngit commit\n\n# 5. Push the updated main back to origin\ngit push origin main\n````\n\nIf you prefer in VS Code’s UI:\n\n1. Open the **Source Control** panel.  \n2. Check out `main` from the branch picker.  \n3. Click the “…” menu → **Merge Branch…** → select your bug branch.  \n4. Resolve conflicts in the editor, stage and commit.  \n5. Click **Publish Changes**.",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
