      "response": [
        {
          "value": "In GitHub’s web UI:\n\n1. Open your pull request.  \n2. Click the green **Merge pull request** ▼ dropdown.  \n3. Choose **Squash and merge**.  \n4. In the edit box, write a single commit message (e.g. “Fixes #123: Correct GUID formatting”), then click **Confirm squash and merge**.  \n5. Optionally click **Delete branch** to clean up.  \n\nIf you prefer the CLI and have the GitHub CLI (`gh`) installed:\n\n```bash\ngh pr merge <PR-number> --squash --delete-branch\n```\n\nOr pure Git:\n\n```bash\n# make sure main is up-to-date\ngit checkout main\ngit pull origin main\n\n# squash your feature branch\ngit merge --squash bug-branch\ngit commit -m \"Fixes #123: Correct GUID formatting\"\n\n# push the squashed main\ngit push origin main\n\n# delete the feature branch remotely\ngit push origin --delete bug-branch\n```",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        }
      ],
      "responseId": "response_947694ab-c2c3-486e-ba70-98f4449c2f2a",
