      "response": [
        {
          "value": "If you merged via the GitHub Pull Requests view in VS Code (the PR extension), that merge happened on the **remote** `origin/main` and you only need to pull it down locally:\n\n```bash\ngit checkout main\ngit pull origin main\n```\n\nIf instead you merged locally in the Source Control tab (using the Merge action there), you’ve created a new commit on your **local** `main`, and you must push it up:\n\n• Click the ⬆️ Push button in the Source Control view  \n  – or –  \n```bash\ngit checkout main\ngit push origin main\n",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        }
