      "response": [
        {
          "value": "Here’s a VS Code–centric flow that keeps your local main clean and in sync:\n\n1. **Stash or Commit Your Local Work**  \n   a) In the Source Control view click the “…” menu → **Stash** → **Stash** (or **Stash All**)  \n   b) OR stage your changes and commit them to a throw‐away “WIP” branch:  \n   • Click the branch picker → **Create new branch** → name it `wip/my-local-changes` → commit.\n\n2. **Pull Down Origin main (including that pending PR merge)**  \n   • Switch to `main` in the branch picker  \n   • Click the “…” menu → **Pull** (or click the 🔄 Sync icon in the status bar)  \n   This fetches and merges whatever’s on `origin/main` into your local `main`.\n\n3. **Merge the Remote PR Locally (if it wasn’t merged on GitHub yet)**  \n   • Open the **GitHub Pull Requests** panel  \n   • Find the pending PR → click **Checkout** to check it out locally  \n   • In the PR panel click **Complete** → **Merge** (or **Squash and merge**)  \n   • Switch back to `main` → “…” → **Pull** again (to bring in that merge commit)\n\n4. **Re-apply Your Local Changes**  \n   a) If you stashed: Source Control “…” → **Stash** → **Pop Stash**  \n   b) If you committed to `wip/...`: checkout your WIP branch, rebase onto `main` or merge it in, resolve conflicts, then commit.\n\n5. **Push Your Updated main**  \n   • Click the ↑ Push button in the status bar (or “…” → **Push**)  \n\nNow your local `main` contains both the collaborator’s PR and your own changes, and it’s in sync with `origin/main`.",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        }
      ],
