          "value": "In VS Code, the GitHub Pull Requests view is provided by the **GitHub Pull Requests and Issues** extension and lives in the Activity Bar:\n\n1. Install/enable **GitHub Pull Requests and Issues**.  \n2. In the left-hand Activity Bar (where Explorer, Search, Source Control, Debug live) you’ll see a GitHub icon (octocat).  \n3. Click that icon to open the **PULL REQUESTS** panel.  \n\nIf you don’t see it, press Ctrl + Shift + P (Cmd + Shift + P on Mac), then run:\n```text\n> GitHub: View Pull Requests and Issues\n```",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
