              "response": "Here are two ways to merge your local feature branch back into your local main:\n\n````bash\n# 1. Make sure you’ve committed or stashed all changes on your feature branch\ngit status\n\n# 2. Switch to main\ngit checkout main\n\n# 3. (Optional) Update main from origin if you track it\ngit pull origin main\n\n# 4. Merge your feature branch into main\ngit merge your-feature-branch\n\n# 5. Resolve any conflicts, then stage & commit the result\n\n# 6. (Optional) Push the updated main back to origin\ngit push origin main\n````\n\nOr via VS Code’s Source Control UI:\n\n1. In the **Status Bar**, click the current-branch name → select **main**.  \n2. Open the **…** menu in the Source Control panel → **Merge Branch…** → choose your feature branch.  \n3. Resolve conflicts in the editor, then click the ✓ (stage) and commit.  \n4. Click the ⬆️ Push button in the Status Bar (if you want to update origin/main).",
