          "value": "You can use `git diff` to compare the two branch heads. For example:\n\n````bash\n# ensure you have up-to-date refs\ngit fetch origin\n\n# show full diff between main and temp\ngit diff origin/main..origin/temp\n\n# or, if both branches are local and up-to-date\ngit diff main..temp\n\n# to see only which files changed\ngit diff --name-status main..temp\n``` ````# ensure you have up-to-date refs\ngit fetch origin\n\n# show full diff between main and temp\ngit diff origin/main..origin/temp\n\n# or, if both branches are local and up-to-date\ngit diff main..temp\n\n# to see only which files changed\ngit diff --name-status main..temp\n",
