      "response": [
        {
          "value": "When you click “Merge” in the GitHub PR or VS Code Git view it opens a temporary commit‐message editor. If you close that file before committing, subsequent clicks can’t find it. You have two options to continue:\n\n1. Re-open the merge commit editor  \n   • Open the Command Palette (Ctrl + Shift + P)  \n   • Run **Git: Open Merge Commit Message**  \n   This will pop the editor back up so you can finalize the message and save/close to complete the merge.\n\n2. Finish the merge manually in the terminal  \n   • In VS Code’s integrated terminal run:  \n   ````bash  \n   git status               # you’ll see “All conflicts fixed but you are still merging.”  \n   git commit               # uses the merge message saved in .git/COMMIT_EDITMSG  \n   ````  \n\nEither approach will complete the merge into your local main.",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
