      "response": [
        {
          "value": "If another app has stolen Ctrl + Shift + P, you can still open the Command Palette in VS Code:\n\n1. Press F1  \n2. Or use the menu: **View → Command Palette…**\n\nIf you want to restore Ctrl + Shift + P, redefine it in your user keybindings:\n\n````jsonc\n[\n  {\n    \"key\": \"ctrl+shift+p\",\n    \"command\": \"workbench.action.showCommands\",\n    \"when\": \"editorTextFocus\"\n  }\n]\n````\n\n– Save that file, then Ctrl + Shift + P will once again open the palette.",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        }
      ],
