              "code": "[\n  {\n    \"key\": \"ctrl+shift+p\",\n    \"command\": \"workbench.action.showCommands\",\n    \"when\": \"editorTextFocus\"\n  }\n]\n",
              "language": "jsonc",
              "markdownBeforeBlock": "If another app has stolen Ctrl + Shift + P, you can still open the Command Palette in VS Code:\n\n1. Press F1  \n2. Or use the menu: **View → Command Palette…**\n\nIf you want to restore Ctrl + Shift + P, redefine it in your user keybindings:\n\n"
            }
          ],
          "toolCallRounds": [
            {
              "response": "If another app has stolen Ctrl + Shift + P, you can still open the Command Palette in VS Code:\n\n1. Press F1  \n2. Or use the menu: **View → Command Palette…**\n\nIf you want to restore Ctrl + Shift + P, redefine it in your user keybindings:\n\n````jsonc\n// filepath: %APPDATA%\\Code\\User\\keybindings.json\n[\n  {\n    \"key\": \"ctrl+shift+p\",\n    \"command\": \"workbench.action.showCommands\",\n    \"when\": \"editorTextFocus\"\n  }\n]\n````\n\n– Save that file, then Ctrl + Shift + P will once again open the palette.",
