            "automaticallyAdded": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "response": [
        {
          "value": "In VS Code (with the GitHub Pull Requests & Issues extension):\n\n1. Click the GitHub icon in the Activity Bar to open the **Pull Requests** view.  \n2. Select your PR from the list.  \n3. In the PR detail pane that opens, click the **Comments** (speech-bubble) tab.  \n   – You’ll see all of your review comments and threads there, grouped by file or by the overall “Conversation.”\n\nAlternatively:\n\n• On GitHub itself, open your repo → **Pull requests** → click your PR → view your notes under the **Conversation** or **Files changed** tabs.  \n• From the CLI (with `gh` installed):  \n```bash\ngh pr view <PR-number> --comments\n```",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        }
      ],
      "responseId": "response_d9339445-39af-4f66-a6cb-bb4b34840504",
      "result": {
        "timings": {
          "firstProgress": 5220,
          "totalElapsed": 6304
        },
        "metadata": {
          "codeBlocks": [
            {
              "code": "gh pr view <PR-number> --comments\n",
              "language": "bash",
              "markdownBeforeBlock": "In VS Code (with the GitHub Pull Requests & Issues extension):\n\n1. Click the GitHub icon in the Activity Bar to open the **Pull Requests** view.  \n2. Select your PR from the list.  \n3. In the PR detail pane that opens, click the **Comments** (speech-bubble) tab.  \n   – You’ll see all of your review comments and threads there, grouped by file or by the overall “Conversation.”\n\nAlternatively:\n\n• On GitHub itself, open your repo → **Pull requests** → click your PR → view your notes under the **Conversation** or **Files changed** tabs.  \n• From the CLI (with `gh` installed):  \n"
            }
          ],
