          "value": "In the **GitHub Pull Requests** view you can toggle from “Open” to “Closed” (or “All”) and then open any PR—even ones already merged or closed—to read its comments.\n\n1. In VS Code’s Activity Bar click the GitHub icon to open the **PULL REQUESTS** panel.  \n2. At the top of that panel you’ll see a drop-down or tabs labeled **Open**, **Closed**, **All**.  \n3. Select **Closed** (or **All**).  \n4. Click the PR you’re interested in to open its detail view, then switch to the **Comments** tab to see all your notes and review threads.\n\nIf you don’t see those filters:\n\n- Run the Command Palette (F1 or View → Command Palette…)  \n- Start typing `GitHub: View Pull Requests` and choose **View All Pull Requests**  \n- Use the same **Open/Closed/All** controls in the list that appears.\n\n---\n\nAlternatively, with the GitHub CLI you can:\n\n````bash\n# list closed PRs\ngh pr list --state closed\n\n# view a specific PR and its comments\ngh pr view 123 --comments\n````",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        }
