      "response": [
        {
          "value": "VS Code’s Copilot Chat “Show Chats” panel is scoped to the current workspace, not globally across all of your repos.  That means:\n\n• If you open Repo A in VS Code, you’ll only see the Copilot chat threads you’ve run in that workspace.  \n• If you switch to Repo B (or a different multi-root workspace), the chat panel will be empty (or show only the threads for that workspace).  \n\nThere is a Copilot Chat setting you can tweak if you’d rather share history across workspaces:\n\n1. Open Settings (Ctrl +, or F1 → “Preferences: Open Settings”).  \n2. Search for “chat history location”.  \n3. Toggle **GitHub Copilot > Chat: History Location** between  \n   – **workspace** (default)  \n   – **global**  \n\nWith **workspace**, chats are tied to that folder/.code-workspace. With **global**, you’ll see the same threads no matter which repo you have open.",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        }
      ],
